fact WorkItem(id: "WI-340", description: some(value: "Scaland follow-on: AnthillParser.scala (line ~414, typeExprToRef) still lowers TypeExpr.Arrow to arrow(effects: cons-list, ...), diverging from the post-WI-307 / WI-331 Rust loader shape (effects: effects_rows(EffectExpression) as a singular Type) and from the stdlib schema. Today this is LATENT — scaland has no operation loading or native typer (per memory: scaland-no-operation-loading.md), so nothing consumes the malformed arrow term and no test catches the divergence. The pre-existing WI-288 test (ParseTest.scala:471) only asserts the arrow functor name 'anthill.prelude.Type.arrow', not the effects-field shape. SCOPE: update AnthillParser.typeExprToRef to construct effects as the canonical effects_rows(EffectExpression) wrapper (the Scala port of build_canonical_effects_rows), matching the Rust loader. The Scala-side EffectExpression entity builders need to be added (parallel to Rust make_effect_expression_*). Add a ParseTest assertion that checks the effects field shape (effects_rows wrapper + inner merge chain) on a 2-effect arrow type, not just the arrow functor name. Will become a blocker once scaland gains operation loading (WI-292 / WI-294). ACCEPTANCE: scaland arrow terms match Rust shape; new ParseTest asserts effects_rows; existing tests still green. (depends: WI-307, WI-331)"), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "scaland-sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-09T19:01:01Z"))
